    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date, returning **400 Bad Request**, following the codebase's existing conventions.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`InvalidRegistrationDateException.java`** (new) \u2014 a concrete subclass of the existing `InvalidOwnerFieldException` base type, which `ExceptionControllerAdvice` already maps uniformly to 400 Bad Request. It carries the client-facing detail while its message provides logging context, exactly like the sibling `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `rejectFutureRegistrationDate(...)` guard invoked inside `normalizeOwnerFields` *before* the date is defaulted or rolled to a business day. It throws the new exception only when a date was supplied (`!= null`) and `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`, so:\n   - A missing date still defaults to the server date.\n   - A past/today date flows through the normal business-day adjustment unchanged.\n   - A future date (e.g. `2999-01-01`) is rejected with 400 before anything is persisted.\n\nThe new acceptance test `errorRejectsFutureDate` passes, and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
